tasks.prompt:
Agent tasks have lifecycle races. Fix them, with a SQL migration where the schema must change (migrations are listed explicitly in `src-tauri/src/db/migrations.rs`; a migration comment must not contain a semicolon):
- hydration completes a queued or running task only when there is an assistant reply newer than the latest user message;
- the runtime placeholder moves status only by guarded transitions (queued to running, running to paused), so it never resurrects a task cancelled in flight;
- the status repair completes only stale queued or running tasks whose latest message is the assistant's, leaving paused and waiting_for_user tasks alone;
- hydrated messages carry the runtime's message identity in a new `agent_messages.external_id` column, unique per task, inserted with INSERT OR IGNORE so overlapping hydrations cannot duplicate a message; the migration removes existing duplicates before creating the unique index.
The repository methods live in `src-tauri/src/db/repositories.rs`.

